IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 (Cth), with the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Regulations 1994 that
-- set its ages, conditions and forms -- when a fund member can take their super out (the conditions of release and cashing
-- restrictions, preservation age, retirement, permanent incapacity), what insurance cover the fund must or may not give them
-- (ss 68AA, 68AAA-68AAD), and who gets it when they die (dependants and legal personal representatives, s 10; the binding death
-- benefit nomination, s 59(1A) and reg 6.17A; to whom, and in what form, a death benefit may be cashed, regs 6.21, 6.22).
--
-- SEAT: the fund member. Every decision is phrased as the member would ask it: "When can I take my super out?", "Must my fund
-- give me death and incapacity cover?", "Is my binding nomination still in effect?", "May my death benefit go to this person?".
-- Where the law addresses only the trustee (s 59, s 62, s 64, ss 68AA-68AAC, regs 6.17A, 6.21, 6.22), the decision says what
-- that means for the member. Where the law hands a judgment to the trustee (permanent incapacity, reg 1.03C; an intention never
-- to work again, reg 6.01(7); severe financial hardship, reg 6.01(5)), the answer is conditional on it, asked as a fact.
--
-- Provisions covered. Act: s 10(1) ("dependant", "spouse", "child", "legal personal representative", "permanent incapacity"),
-- s 10A(1), (2), s 29WA(1), (2), (4), s 59(1), (1A), (2), s 62(1)(a), (b), s 64(1), (2), s 68AA(1), (5), (8A), (8B), (9),
-- s 68AAA(1), (3)-(6), s 68AAB(1), (3), (4), s 68AAC(1)-(4), s 68AAD. Regulations: reg 1.03C (permanent incapacity), reg 6.01(2)
-- ("preservation age", "condition of release", "cashing restriction", "temporary incapacity"), (5) (severe financial hardship),
-- (7) (retirement), reg 6.01A (terminal medical condition), reg 6.15(1), reg 6.18(1), (3), reg 6.17A(2)-(7), reg 6.21(1),
-- (2A), (2C), reg 6.22(1)-(3), reg 13.18, and Schedule 1 Part 1 items 101, 102, 102A, 103, 105, 106, 108, 109, 110.
--
-- Edition: Act -- Compilation No. 131, compilation date 10 August 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 49, 2026, as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04633.txt. Regulations -- Compilation No. 159, compilation date 1 July 2026,
-- includes amendments F2026L00133 (register id F2026C00541), as deposited at
-- ../../../superannuation-industry-supervision-regulations-1994/registers/source-bundle/F1996B00580.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: RSE licensing, MySuper authorisation, covenants (s 52), investment rules, Parts 8 to 32; the successor-fund
-- transfer of insurance elections (ss 68AAA(2A), 68AAB(3A)-(3C), 68AAC(3A)-(3C)); the conditions of the employer-sponsor and
-- dangerous occupation exceptions (ss 68AAE, 68AAF -- each asked as a fact); s 29WA(6); the penalties; restricted and
-- unrestricted non-preserved benefits (regs 6.10-6.13, 6.19, 6.20: every contribution is taken to be preserved, reg 6.15(1));
-- temporary residents (reg 6.01B); Schedule 1 items 103A, 103B, 104, 107, 107A, 109A, 111-114 and Part 2 (approved deposit
-- funds); compassionate grounds (reg 6.19A); the amount and timing caps in reg 6.18(2), (4); reg 6.21(2B) (a child's pension
-- commuted at 25); reg 6.22(4)-(6). Choice of fund, the stapled fund and the 11% contribution rate are in the Superannuation
-- Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992, not here. The tax on a death benefit is the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 Div 302.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual
-- to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 -- the fund member`

§§ `dates and ages`

GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
      `on`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`age in completed years` MEANS
    IF     DATE_MONTH `on` GREATER THAN DATE_MONTH `born on`
        OR (DATE_MONTH `on` EQUALS DATE_MONTH `born on` AND DATE_DAY `on` AT LEAST DATE_DAY `born on`)
    THEN DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born on`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born on` MINUS 1

-- The same day and month, a number of years later. (A 29 February start is carried into March by the date library.)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
      `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day years later` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `the date`) (DATE_MONTH `the date`) (DATE_YEAR `the date` PLUS `years`)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is on or before` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

-- Reg 6.01(2): "preservation age means: (a) for a person born before 1 July 1960--55 years; (b) ... 1 July 1960 to 30 June
-- 1961--56 years; (c) ... 1 July 1961 to 30 June 1962--57 years; (d) ... 1 July 1962 to 30 June 1963--58 years; (e) ... 1 July
-- 1963 to 30 June 1964--59 years; or (f) for a person born after 30 June 1964--60 years."
-- Gloss: the age from which a member may begin to draw on preserved super in a restricted form (Schedule 1 item 110), and the
-- floor for "retirement" in reg 6.01(7)(a).
@export What is my preservation age (SIS Regulations reg 6.01(2))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my preservation age` IS
    BRANCH IF DATE_SERIAL `my date of birth` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 7 1960) THEN 55
           IF DATE_SERIAL `my date of birth` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 7 1961) THEN 56
           IF DATE_SERIAL `my date of birth` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 7 1962) THEN 57
           IF DATE_SERIAL `my date of birth` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 7 1963) THEN 58
           IF DATE_SERIAL `my date of birth` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 7 1964) THEN 59
           OTHERWISE 60

-- Reg 13.18: "For the purposes of subparagraph 62(1)(a)(ii) of the Act, 65 years is the specified age."
`the age specified for the sole purpose test` MEANS 65

§§ `10, 10A -- my dependants and my legal personal representative`

-- s 10(1): "dependant, in relation to a person, includes the spouse of the person, any child of the person and any person with
-- whom the person has an interdependency relationship." "spouse of a person includes: (a)" a person in a relationship registered
-- under a prescribed State or Territory law; "(b) another person who, although not legally married to the person, lives with the
-- person on a genuine domestic basis in a relationship as a couple." "child, in relation to a person, includes: (a) an adopted
-- child, a stepchild or an ex-nuptial child of the person; and (b) a child of the person's spouse; and (c)" a child within the
-- Family Law Act 1975.
-- s 10A(1): an interdependency relationship if "(a) they have a close personal relationship; and (b) they live together; and (c)
-- one or each of them provides the other with financial support; and (d) one or each of them provides the other with domestic
-- support and personal care"; (2): or (a) alone, where they fail the others because of "a physical, intellectual or psychiatric
-- disability".
--
-- Every definition says "includes". A legally married spouse is read as a spouse in the ordinary sense (INFERENCE: the list
-- mentions marriage only to say a de facto partner is "not legally married"). A dependant only in the ordinary (financial) sense
-- is asked as a fact; the Act does not define that sense. No age limit attaches to "child": an adult child is a dependant.
DECLARE `A person` HAS
    `is legally married to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in a registered relationship with me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lives with me on a genuine domestic basis as a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is my child, adopted child, stepchild or ex-nuptial child, or a child of my spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a close personal relationship with me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of us gives the other financial support` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of us gives the other domestic support and personal care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fails those other tests only because of a disability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is financially dependent on me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age in years` IS A NUMBER
    `has a permanent disability needing ongoing support, as reg 6.21(2C) describes` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is my spouse` IF
        `the person`'s `is legally married to me`
    OR  `the person`'s `is in a registered relationship with me`
    OR  `the person`'s `lives with me on a genuine domestic basis as a couple`

GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has an interdependency relationship with me` IF
        `the person`'s `has a close personal relationship with me`
    AND (    (    `the person`'s `lives with me`
              AND `the person`'s `one of us gives the other financial support`
              AND `the person`'s `one of us gives the other domestic support and personal care`)
         OR  `the person`'s `fails those other tests only because of a disability`)

@export Is this person my dependant (SIS Act s 10(1), s 10A)?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person` @desc The person and their relationship to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person my dependant` IF
        `is my spouse` `the person`
    OR  `the person`'s `is my child, adopted child, stepchild or ex-nuptial child, or a child of my spouse`
    OR  `has an interdependency relationship with me` `the person`
    OR  `the person`'s `is financially dependent on me`

-- s 10(1): "legal personal representative means the executor of the will or administrator of the estate of a deceased person,
-- the trustee of the estate of a person under a legal disability or a person who holds an enduring power of attorney granted by
-- a person."
DECLARE `An office` IS ONE OF
    `executor of my will`
    `administrator of my estate`
    `trustee of my estate while I am under a legal disability`
    `holder of an enduring power of attorney I granted`
    `holder of an ordinary power of attorney`
    `no office`

@export Is this person my legal personal representative (SIS Act s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the office` IS AN `An office` @desc The office the person holds for you, if any
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person my legal personal representative` IF
    CONSIDER `the office`
    WHEN `holder of an ordinary power of attorney` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no office` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Schedule 1, regs 6.01, 6.18, 1.03C -- when can I take my super out`

-- Reg 6.15(1): contributions "are taken to be preserved benefits ... unless and until the trustee is satisfied that they are
-- not". Reg 6.18(1): "A member's preserved benefits ... may be cashed on or after the satisfaction by the member of a condition
-- of release." Reg 6.01(2): "condition of release means a condition of release specified in Column 2 of Schedule 1 and ... a
-- member ... is taken to have satisfied a condition of release if the event specified in that condition has occurred".
-- Schedule 1 Part 1 (regulated superannuation funds), the items a member in this seat meets:
DECLARE `A condition of release` IS ONE OF
    `retirement`                                              -- item 101
    `death`                                                   -- item 102
    `terminal medical condition`                              -- item 102A
    `permanent incapacity`                                    -- item 103
    `severe financial hardship`                               -- item 105
    `attaining age 65`                                        -- item 106
    `leaving a job with an employer who contributed for me`   -- item 108
    `temporary incapacity`                                    -- item 109
    `attaining preservation age`                              -- item 110

`every condition of release encoded` MEANS
    LIST `retirement`, `death`, `terminal medical condition`, `permanent incapacity`, `severe financial hardship`,
         `attaining age 65`, `leaving a job with an employer who contributed for me`, `temporary incapacity`,
         `attaining preservation age`

-- Column 3, "cashing restrictions": the form in which preserved benefits may be cashed (reg 6.18(3)). "Nil" means "any 1 or more
-- of ... lump sums ... pensions ... annuities" (reg 6.18(3)(b)).
DECLARE `A cashing restriction` IS ONE OF
    `nil: any lump sums, pensions or annuities`
    `a single lump sum of $1,000 to $10,000 in each 12 months`
    `a non-commutable life pension or life annuity only`
    `an income stream replacing my pay, for the period of incapacity only`
    `a transition to retirement or other non-commutable income stream only`

DECLARE `My circumstances` HAS
    `my date of birth` IS A DATE
    `today` IS A DATE
    `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an employment arrangement of mine has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date it ended` IS A DATE
    `that employer contributed to the fund for me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee is reasonably satisfied I intend never again to be gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee is reasonably satisfied my ill-health makes work I am qualified for unlikely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ill-health made me stop work, but it is not permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `two doctors, one a specialist, certify I am likely to die within 24 months, and that period has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have had income support for 26 continuous weeks and still have it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee is satisfied I cannot meet reasonable and immediate family living expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had income support for 39 weeks in all after reaching my preservation age` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my age today` MEANS `age in completed years` (`me`'s `my date of birth`) (`me`'s `today`)

-- Reg 6.01(7): "the retirement of a person is taken to occur: (a) in the case of a person who has reached a preservation age
-- that is less than 60--if: (i) an arrangement under which the member was gainfully employed has come to an end; and (ii) the
-- trustee is reasonably satisfied that the person intends never to again become gainfully employed, either on a full-time or a
-- part-time basis; or (b) in the case of a person who has attained the age of 60--an arrangement under which the member was
-- gainfully employed has come to an end, and either of the following circumstances apply: (i) the person attained that age on
-- or before the ending of the employment; or (ii) the trustee is reasonably satisfied that the person intends never to again
-- become gainfully employed".
-- Gloss: at 60 or over, leaving ANY job held at 60 is retirement, even if another job continues ("an arrangement"). Below
-- preservation age, no one has retired for Schedule 1.
@export Have I retired, as the SIS Regulations define it (reg 6.01(7))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your age, work and the trustee's views
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I retired` IF
    BRANCH IF `my age today` `me` AT LEAST 60
           THEN     `me`'s `an employment arrangement of mine has ended`
                AND (    `age in completed years` (`me`'s `my date of birth`) (`me`'s `the date it ended`) AT LEAST 60
                     OR  `me`'s `the trustee is reasonably satisfied I intend never again to be gainfully employed`)
           IF `my age today` `me` AT LEAST `What is my preservation age` (`me`'s `my date of birth`)
           THEN     `me`'s `an employment arrangement of mine has ended`
                AND `me`'s `the trustee is reasonably satisfied I intend never again to be gainfully employed`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Reg 6.01(5): severe financial hardship if "(a) the trustee ... is satisfied ... that: (A) the person has received
-- Commonwealth income support payments for a continuous period of 26 weeks; and (B) the person was in receipt of payments of
-- that kind on the date of the written evidence; and (ii) that the person is unable to meet reasonable and immediate family
-- living expenses; or (b) the person has reached the age that is the person's preservation age plus 39 weeks and the trustee
-- ... is satisfied: (i) ... that the person received Commonwealth income support payments for a cumulative period of 39 weeks
-- after the person reached the person's preservation age; and (ii) that the person was not gainfully employed".
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am in hardship under reg 6.01(5)(a)` IF
        `me`'s `I have had income support for 26 continuous weeks and still have it`
    AND `me`'s `the trustee is satisfied I cannot meet reasonable and immediate family living expenses`

GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day I reach preservation age plus 39 weeks` MEANS
    `serial plus` (DATE_SERIAL (`the same day years later` (`me`'s `my date of birth`) (`What is my preservation age` (`me`'s `my date of birth`)))) 273

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
      `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`serial plus` MEANS `x` PLUS `y`

GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am in hardship under reg 6.01(5)(b)` IF
        DATE_SERIAL (`me`'s `today`) AT LEAST `the day I reach preservation age plus 39 weeks` `me`
    AND `me`'s `I had income support for 39 weeks in all after reaching my preservation age`
    AND (NOT `me`'s `I am gainfully employed`)

-- s 10(1): "permanent incapacity" if "the member is taken, under the regulations, to be suffering permanent incapacity". Reg
-- 1.03C: "if a trustee of the fund is reasonably satisfied that the member's ill-health (whether physical or mental) makes it
-- unlikely that the member will engage in gainful employment for which the member is reasonably qualified by education,
-- training or experience." No age attaches.
-- Reg 6.01A: a terminal medical condition exists if two registered medical practitioners (at least one a specialist in the
-- area) certify an illness or injury "likely to result in the death of the person within a period ... that ends not more than
-- 24 months after the date of the certification", and the certification period has not ended (one fact here).
-- Reg 6.01(2): "temporary incapacity ... means ill-health ... that caused the member to cease to be gainfully employed but does
-- not constitute permanent incapacity."
@export Have I met this condition of release (SIS Regulations Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `the condition` IS A `A condition of release` @desc The condition of release in Schedule 1
      `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your age, work, health and the trustee's views
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met this condition of release` IF
    CONSIDER `the condition`
    WHEN `retirement` THEN `Have I retired` `me`
    WHEN `death` THEN `me`'s `I have died`
    WHEN `terminal medical condition` THEN
        `me`'s `two doctors, one a specialist, certify I am likely to die within 24 months, and that period has not ended`
    WHEN `permanent incapacity` THEN
        `me`'s `the trustee is reasonably satisfied my ill-health makes work I am qualified for unlikely`
    WHEN `severe financial hardship` THEN
        `I am in hardship under reg 6.01(5)(a)` `me` OR `I am in hardship under reg 6.01(5)(b)` `me`
    WHEN `attaining age 65` THEN `my age today` `me` AT LEAST 65
    WHEN `leaving a job with an employer who contributed for me` THEN
        `me`'s `an employment arrangement of mine has ended` AND `me`'s `that employer contributed to the fund for me`
    WHEN `temporary incapacity` THEN
            `me`'s `ill-health made me stop work, but it is not permanent`
        AND (NOT `me`'s `the trustee is reasonably satisfied my ill-health makes work I am qualified for unlikely`)
    WHEN `attaining preservation age` THEN
        `my age today` `me` AT LEAST `What is my preservation age` (`me`'s `my date of birth`)

-- Schedule 1 Part 1, column 3, for preserved benefits: items 101, 102, 102A, 103, 106 "Nil"; item 105 "(a)--in each 12 month
-- period ... a single lump sum not less than $1,000 ... and not more than $10,000" and "(b)--Nil"; item 108 "Preserved
-- benefits: Non-commutable life pension or non-commutable life annuity"; item 109 "A non-commutable income stream ... for (a)
-- the purpose of continuing ... the gain or reward ... and (b) a period not exceeding the period of incapacity"; item 110 "(a) a
-- transition to retirement income stream; (b) a non-commutable allocated annuity; (c) a non-commutable allocated pension; (d) a
-- non-commutable annuity; (e) a non-commutable pension".
@export In what form may I take my preserved super under this condition of release (SIS Regulations Schedule 1, reg 6.18(3))?
GIVEN `the condition` IS A `A condition of release` @desc The condition of release in Schedule 1
      `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances (they decide which limb of severe financial hardship applies)
GIVETH A `A cashing restriction`
DECIDE `In what form may I take my super under this condition` IS
    CONSIDER `the condition`
    WHEN `severe financial hardship` THEN
        IF `I am in hardship under reg 6.01(5)(b)` `me`
        THEN `nil: any lump sums, pensions or annuities`
        ELSE `a single lump sum of $1,000 to $10,000 in each 12 months`
    WHEN `leaving a job with an employer who contributed for me` THEN `a non-commutable life pension or life annuity only`
    WHEN `temporary incapacity` THEN `an income stream replacing my pay, for the period of incapacity only`
    WHEN `attaining preservation age` THEN `a transition to retirement or other non-commutable income stream only`
    OTHERWISE `nil: any lump sums, pensions or annuities`

@export Can I draw on my preserved super at all now (SIS Regulations reg 6.18(1))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your age, work, health and the trustee's views
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I draw on my super now` IF
    any (GIVEN c YIELD `Have I met this condition of release` c `me`) `every condition of release encoded`

-- A condition met whose cashing restriction is "Nil" lets the member take everything, in any form, including a lump sum.
@export Can I take all my preserved super, in any form including a lump sum, now (SIS Regulations Schedule 1, reg 6.18(3)(b))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your age, work, health and the trustee's views
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I take all my super in any form now` IF
    any (GIVEN c YIELD     `Have I met this condition of release` c `me`
                       AND `In what form may I take my super under this condition` c `me` EQUALS `nil: any lump sums, pensions or annuities`)
        `every condition of release encoded`

§§ `59, reg 6.17A -- my binding death benefit nomination`

-- s 59(1): "Subject to subsection (1A), the governing rules of a superannuation entity other than a self managed superannuation
-- fund must not permit a discretion ... exercisable by a person other than a trustee ... to be exercised unless: (a) those rules
-- require the consent of the trustee" or (b) in an employer-sponsored fund, the discretion relates to the employer-sponsor's
-- contributions, solely to terminating the fund, or circumstances covered by regulations. (2): inconsistent rules are "to the
-- extent of the inconsistency, invalid".
@export Can my fund's rules let someone other than the trustee make this decision about my benefits (SIS Act s 59(1))?
GIVEN `is a self managed superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your fund is a self managed superannuation fund
      `the rules require the trustee's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rules make the decision subject to the trustee's consent
      `is an employer-sponsored fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund is employer-sponsored
      `relates to employer contributions, termination, or a case the regulations cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is about the employer's contributions, solely about ending the fund, or a case covered by regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can someone other than the trustee make this decision` IF
        `is a self managed superannuation fund`
    OR  `the rules require the trustee's consent`
    OR  (    `is an employer-sponsored fund`
         AND `relates to employer contributions, termination, or a case the regulations cover`)

-- s 59(1A): "Despite subsection (1), the governing rules of a superannuation entity may, subject to a trustee of the entity
-- complying with any conditions contained in the regulations, permit a member of the entity, by notice given to a trustee of the
-- entity in accordance with the regulations, to require a trustee of the entity to provide any benefits in respect of the member
-- on or after the member's death to a person or persons mentioned in the notice, being the legal personal representative or a
-- dependant or dependants of the member."
-- Reg 6.17A(2): the rules may so permit "if the trustee gives to the member information under subregulation (3)" -- (3):
-- "information that the trustee reasonably believes the member reasonably needs for the purpose of understanding the right".
@export May I name this person in a binding death benefit nomination (SIS Act s 59(1A), reg 6.17A(4)(a))?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person` @desc The person and their relationship to you
      `the office` IS AN `An office` @desc The office the person holds for you, if any
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I name this person in a binding nomination` IF
        `Is this person my dependant` `the person`
    OR  `Is this person my legal personal representative` `the office`

-- Reg 6.17A(6): the notice "(a) must be in writing; and (b) must be signed, and dated, by the member in the presence of 2
-- witnesses, being persons: (i) each of whom has turned 18; and (ii) neither of whom is a person mentioned in the notice; and
-- (c) must contain a declaration signed, and dated, by the witnesses stating that the notice was signed by the member in their
-- presence." (4)(b): "the proportion of the benefit that will be paid to that person, or to each of those persons, is certain
-- or readily ascertainable from the notice".
DECLARE `My nomination notice` HAS
    `is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I signed and dated it in front of two witnesses` IS A BOOLEAN
    `both witnesses had turned 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `neither witness is named in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witnesses signed and dated a declaration that I signed in their presence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each person's share is certain or readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day I first signed it, or last confirmed or amended it` IS A DATE
    `I have revoked it` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is my nomination notice made in the form the regulations require (SIS Regulations reg 6.17A(6), (4)(b))?
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `My nomination notice` @desc How your nomination was made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my nomination notice in proper form` IF
        `the notice`'s `is in writing`
    AND `the notice`'s `I signed and dated it in front of two witnesses`
    AND `the notice`'s `both witnesses had turned 18`
    AND `the notice`'s `neither witness is named in it`
    AND `the notice`'s `the witnesses signed and dated a declaration that I signed in their presence`
    AND `the notice`'s `each person's share is certain or readily ascertainable`

-- Reg 6.17A(7): "Unless sooner revoked by the member, a notice under subregulation (4) ceases to have effect: (a) at the end of
-- the period of 3 years after the day it was first signed, or last confirmed or amended, by the member; or (b) if the governing
-- rules of the fund fix a shorter period--at the end of that period." (5)(a): the member may "confirm the notice by giving to
-- the trustee a written notice, signed, and dated, by the member".
-- The regulations provide NO non-lapsing notice. A nomination a fund calls "non-lapsing" is not a reg 6.17A notice, and this
-- encoding does not decide what binds the trustee under one (whether the rules may give it effect with the trustee's consent
-- under s 59(1)(a) is not answered by the deposited text).
`the period before a nomination lapses, in years` MEANS 3

DECLARE `What has become of my nomination` IS ONE OF
    `in effect`
    `revoked`
    `lapsed at the end of 3 years (reg 6.17A(7)(a))`
    `lapsed at the end of the shorter period my fund's rules fix (reg 6.17A(7)(b))`

@export Is my binding nomination still in effect on this day (SIS Regulations reg 6.17A(7))?
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `My nomination notice` @desc How and when your nomination was made
      `the shorter period my fund's rules fix, in years (0 if none)` IS A NUMBER @desc Any period shorter than 3 years that your fund's rules fix, in years; 0 if none
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about (for a death benefit, the day of death)
GIVETH A `What has become of my nomination`
DECIDE `What has become of my nomination on this day` IS
    BRANCH IF `the notice`'s `I have revoked it` THEN `revoked`
           IF     `the shorter period my fund's rules fix, in years (0 if none)` GREATER THAN 0
              AND `the shorter period my fund's rules fix, in years (0 if none)` LESS THAN `the period before a nomination lapses, in years`
              AND (NOT `is on or before` `the day`
                        (`the same day years later` (`the notice`'s `the day I first signed it, or last confirmed or amended it`)
                                                    `the shorter period my fund's rules fix, in years (0 if none)`))
           THEN `lapsed at the end of the shorter period my fund's rules fix (reg 6.17A(7)(b))`
           IF (NOT `is on or before` `the day`
                    (`the same day years later` (`the notice`'s `the day I first signed it, or last confirmed or amended it`)
                                                `the period before a nomination lapses, in years`))
           THEN `lapsed at the end of 3 years (reg 6.17A(7)(a))`
           OTHERWISE `in effect`

-- Reg 6.17A(4): "if the governing rules of a fund permit [it] ..., the trustee must pay a benefit in respect of the member, on
-- or after the death of the member, to the person or persons mentioned in a notice ... if: (a) the person, or each of the
-- persons, mentioned in the notice is the legal personal representative or a dependant of the member; and (b) the proportion
-- ... is certain or readily ascertainable ...; and (c) the notice is in accordance with subregulation (6); and (d) the notice is
-- in effect." (4A): not if the trustee is under a court order restraining payment, or knows the member is under a court order
-- to amend or revoke the notice or not to give one.
-- One nominee is one case here; for several, ask once for each.
@export When I die, must my fund pay my death benefit to the person my binding nomination names (SIS Act s 59(1A), reg 6.17A(4))?
GIVEN `my fund's rules permit binding nominations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your fund's governing rules allow binding death benefit nominations
      `the trustee gave me the information about my right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee gave you the information reg 6.17A(3) requires
      `the notice` IS A `My nomination notice` @desc How and when your nomination was made
      `the shorter period my fund's rules fix, in years (0 if none)` IS A NUMBER @desc Any period shorter than 3 years that your fund's rules fix, in years; 0 if none
      `the day I die` IS A DATE @desc The day of your death
      `the person` IS A `A person` @desc The person you named and their relationship to you
      `the office` IS AN `An office` @desc The office that person holds for you, if any
      `a court order stands in the way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court order restrains the trustee, or requires you to change or revoke the notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my fund pay my death benefit as my nomination says` IF
        `my fund's rules permit binding nominations`
    AND `the trustee gave me the information about my right`
    AND `May I name this person in a binding nomination` `the person` `the office`
    AND `Is my nomination notice in proper form` `the notice`
    AND `What has become of my nomination on this day` `the notice` `the shorter period my fund's rules fix, in years (0 if none)` `the day I die`
            EQUALS `in effect`
    AND (NOT `a court order stands in the way`)

§§ `regs 6.21, 6.22 -- who may receive my super when I die, and in what form`

-- Reg 6.21(1): "a member's benefits in a regulated superannuation fund must be cashed as soon as practicable after the member
-- dies." Reg 6.22(1)-(3): after death, benefits must not be cashed in favour of anyone other than the member's legal personal
-- representative or "one or more of the member's dependants", unless "(a) the trustee has not, after making reasonable
-- enquiries, found either a legal personal representative, or a dependant, of the member; and (b) the person in whose favour
-- benefits are cashed is an individual."
@export When I die, may my super be paid to this person (SIS Regulations reg 6.22)?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person` @desc The person and their relationship to you
      `the office` IS AN `An office` @desc The office the person holds for you, if any
      `the trustee found no legal personal representative or dependant after reasonable enquiries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee, after reasonable enquiries, found neither your legal personal representative nor any dependant
      `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is an individual (not a company or charity)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my super be paid to this person when I die` IF
        `Is this person my dependant` `the person`
    OR  `Is this person my legal personal representative` `the office`
    OR  (    `the trustee found no legal personal representative or dependant after reasonable enquiries`
         AND `the person is an individual`)

-- Reg 6.21(2A): a death benefit may be paid as a pension or annuity (paras (2)(b)(i), (ii)) "only if, at the time of the
-- member's death, the entitled recipient: (a) is a dependant of the member; and (b) in the case of a child of the member: (i) is
-- less than 18 years of age; or (ii) being 18 or more years of age: (A) is financially dependent on the member and less than 25
-- years of age; or (B) is a person with disability to whom subregulation (2C) applies." Otherwise only a lump sum (2)(a).
@export When I die, may this person take my super as a pension rather than only as a lump sum (SIS Regulations reg 6.21(2A))?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person` @desc The person, their relationship to you and their age when you die
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this person take my super as a pension` IF
        `Is this person my dependant` `the person`
    AND (    (NOT `the person`'s `is my child, adopted child, stepchild or ex-nuptial child, or a child of my spouse`)
         OR  `the person`'s `age in years` LESS THAN 18
         OR  (`the person`'s `is financially dependent on me` AND `the person`'s `age in years` LESS THAN 25)
         OR  `the person`'s `has a permanent disability needing ongoing support, as reg 6.21(2C) describes`)

§§ `62 -- on what occasions my fund may pay me at all`

-- s 62(1)(a), the core purposes: benefits for each member "(i) on or after the member's retirement"; "(ii) on or after the
-- member's attainment of an age not less than the age specified in the regulations" (reg 13.18: 65); (iii) the earlier of the
-- two; "(iv)" and "(v)" benefits on or after the member's death, if it occurred before retirement or before that age, "and the
-- benefits are provided to the member's legal personal representative, to any or all of the member's dependants, or to both".
-- s 62(1)(b), the ancillary purposes: "(i)" on termination of employment with an employer who had contributed; "(ii) on or
-- after the member's cessation of work ... on account of ill-health (whether physical or mental)"; (iii), (iv) death after
-- retirement or after that age, to the legal personal representative or dependants; "(v) such other benefits as the Regulator
-- approves in writing". "Retirement" in s 62 is not defined by reg 6.01(7) (which is "for the purposes of Schedule 1"); it is
-- asked as a fact.
DECLARE `An occasion` IS ONE OF
    `my retirement`
    `reaching age 65`
    `my death`
    `leaving a job with an employer who contributed`
    `stopping work because of ill-health`
    `a benefit the Regulator has approved in writing`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the occasion` IS AN `An occasion`
      `I have retired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `paid to my legal personal representative or dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `serves a core purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the occasion`
    WHEN `my retirement` THEN `I have retired`
    WHEN `reaching age 65` THEN `my age` AT LEAST `the age specified for the sole purpose test`
    WHEN `my death` THEN
            `paid to my legal personal representative or dependants`
        AND (    (NOT `I have retired`)
             OR  `my age` LESS THAN `the age specified for the sole purpose test`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the occasion` IS AN `An occasion`
      `I have retired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `paid to my legal personal representative or dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `serves an ancillary purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the occasion`
    WHEN `leaving a job with an employer who contributed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `stopping work because of ill-health` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a benefit the Regulator has approved in writing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my death` THEN
            `paid to my legal personal representative or dependants`
        AND (    `I have retired`
             OR  `my age` AT LEAST `the age specified for the sole purpose test`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export May my fund be maintained to pay me a benefit on this occasion (SIS Act s 62, reg 13.18)?
GIVEN `the occasion` IS AN `An occasion` @desc The occasion on which the benefit is paid
      `I have retired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have retired
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years at the time (at death, for a death benefit)
      `paid to my legal personal representative or dependants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a death benefit, whether it goes to your legal personal representative or dependants
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my fund pay a benefit on this occasion` IF
        `serves a core purpose` `the occasion` `I have retired` `my age` `paid to my legal personal representative or dependants`
    OR  `serves an ancillary purpose` `the occasion` `I have retired` `my age` `paid to my legal personal representative or dependants`

§§ `29WA, 64 -- where my contributions go, and when deductions from my pay must reach the fund`

-- s 29WA(1)-(2): for a member "other than a defined benefit member", a contribution "in relation to which no direction has been
-- given" must be treated "as a contribution to be paid into a MySuper product of the fund". (4): a direction alleged to have
-- been given after 31 March 2013 "is taken not to have been given if: (a) the direction was not given in writing; or (b) a copy
-- of the direction is not held by or on behalf of the trustee".
@export Does my contribution go into my fund's MySuper product (SIS Act s 29WA)?
GIVEN `I am a defined benefit member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a defined benefit member
      `I gave an investment direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you directed where your contributions are invested
      `the direction was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that direction was in writing
      `the trustee holds a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee holds a copy of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my contribution go into MySuper` IF
        (NOT `I am a defined benefit member`)
    AND (    (NOT `I gave an investment direction`)
         OR  (NOT `the direction was in writing`)
         OR  (NOT `the trustee holds a copy`))

-- s 64(2): where an employer is authorised to deduct an amount from the member's pay and pay it to a regulated fund, "the
-- employer must pay to a trustee of the superannuation fund the amount of the deduction before the end of the 28-day period
-- beginning immediately after the end of the month in which the deduction was made." This is about deductions from pay; the
-- employer's own superannuation guarantee contribution is the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992's.
GIVEN `the deduction day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the next month` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the deduction day` EQUALS 12
    THEN Date 1 1 (DATE_YEAR `the deduction day` PLUS 1)
    ELSE Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `the deduction day` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `the deduction day`)

@export What is the last day by which an amount deducted from my pay must reach my fund (SIS Act s 64(2))?
GIVEN `the deduction day` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount was deducted from your pay
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day my deduction must reach my fund` IS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (`serial plus` (DATE_SERIAL (`the first day of the next month` `the deduction day`)) 27)

@export Did the amount deducted from my pay reach my fund in time (SIS Act s 64(2))?
GIVEN `the deduction day` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount was deducted from your pay
      `the day it was paid to the fund` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer paid it to the trustee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my deduction reach my fund in time` IF
    `is on or before` `the day it was paid to the fund` (`What is the last day my deduction must reach my fund` `the deduction day`)

§§ `68AA, 68AAA-68AAD -- insurance cover inside my super`

-- s 68AAA(1): no benefit by "taking out or maintaining insurance" under a choice or MySuper product if "(a) the member's account
-- is inactive ... for a continuous period of 16 months" and the member has not elected cover under (2). (3): inactive = the
-- trustee has "not received an amount in respect of the member" in the period; (4), (5): the bar lifts when an amount is received
-- and returns after another 16 months. (6): not for (a) a defined benefit member, (b), (c) permanent or continuous full-time ADF
-- Super members, "(d) a member to whom the employer-sponsor contribution exception applies".
-- s 68AAB(1): the same bar if "(a) the member has an account balance ... less than $6,000; and (b) on or after 1 November 2019,
-- the member has not had an account balance ... equal to or greater than $6,000" and no election. (3): an election under s
-- 68AAC(2) counts. (4): exclusions (a)-(d) and "(e) a member to whom the dangerous occupation exception applies".
-- s 68AAC(1): the same bar if "(a) the member is under the age of 25 years" and no election. (2): each member under 25 "may
-- elect, in writing". (3): an election under s 68AAB(2) counts. (4): exclusions (a)-(e).
-- s 68AAD: ss 68AAA-68AAC "do not apply in relation to regulated superannuation funds with no more than 6 members".
-- The dangerous occupation exception (s 68AAF) is in the exclusions of ss 68AAB and 68AAC but NOT of s 68AAA.
DECLARE `My account` HAS
    `my fund has no more than 6 members` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a defined benefit member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a permanent or continuous full-time ADF Super member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer-sponsor contribution exception applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dangerous occupation exception applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my age in years` IS A NUMBER
    `months since the fund last received an amount for me` IS A NUMBER
    `my balance` IS A NUMBER
    `my balance has been $6,000 or more since 1 November 2019` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I elected in writing to keep cover though inactive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I elected in writing to have cover though my balance is low` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I elected in writing to have cover though under 25` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a MySuper product` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I elected not to have death and incapacity cover` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `outside ss 68AAA-68AAC altogether` IF
        `the account`'s `my fund has no more than 6 members`
    OR  `the account`'s `I am a defined benefit member`
    OR  `the account`'s `I am a permanent or continuous full-time ADF Super member`
    OR  `the account`'s `the employer-sponsor contribution exception applies to me`

GIVEN `the account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 68AAA bars cover for an inactive account` IF
        (NOT `outside ss 68AAA-68AAC altogether` `the account`)
    AND `the account`'s `months since the fund last received an amount for me` AT LEAST 16
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `I elected in writing to keep cover though inactive`)

GIVEN `the account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 68AAB bars cover for a low balance` IF
        (NOT `outside ss 68AAA-68AAC altogether` `the account`)
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `the dangerous occupation exception applies to me`)
    AND `the account`'s `my balance` LESS THAN 6000
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `my balance has been $6,000 or more since 1 November 2019`)
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `I elected in writing to have cover though my balance is low`)
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `I elected in writing to have cover though under 25`)

GIVEN `the account` IS A `My account`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 68AAC bars cover for a member under 25` IF
        (NOT `outside ss 68AAA-68AAC altogether` `the account`)
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `the dangerous occupation exception applies to me`)
    AND `the account`'s `my age in years` LESS THAN 25
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `I elected in writing to have cover though under 25`)
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `I elected in writing to have cover though my balance is low`)

@export May my fund give me insurance cover through my super (SIS Act ss 68AAA-68AAD)?
GIVEN `the account` IS A `My account` @desc Your account, age, balance and any elections you have made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my fund give me insurance cover` IF
        (NOT `s 68AAA bars cover for an inactive account` `the account`)
    AND (NOT `s 68AAB bars cover for a low balance` `the account`)
    AND (NOT `s 68AAC bars cover for a member under 25` `the account`)

-- s 68AAC(2): the trustee "must ensure that each member ... who is under the age of 25 years may elect, in writing" to have
-- cover. s 68AAB(2) and s 68AAA(2) give the same right to any member of a choice or MySuper product.
@export Am I entitled to elect in writing to have insurance cover despite being under 25 (SIS Act s 68AAC(2))?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to elect cover though under 25` IF
    `my age in years` LESS THAN 25

-- s 68AA(1): each trustee must ensure "(a) that the fund provides permanent incapacity benefit to each MySuper member"; "(b) ...
-- death benefit"; "(c) ... by taking out insurance". (5): each MySuper member may elect that either or both "will not be
-- provided". (8A), (8B): no requirement where s 68AAA, 68AAB or 68AAC stops it being provided by insurance. (9): not for a
-- defined benefit member or a permanent or continuous full-time ADF Super member. (2), (3): reasonable conditions the trustee
-- determines (for example, the policy's terms) are outside this encoding. Income protection (temporary incapacity cover) is not
-- required by s 68AA: it names only death and permanent incapacity benefit.
@export Must my fund give me default death and permanent incapacity cover (SIS Act s 68AA)?
GIVEN `the account` IS A `My account` @desc Your account, age, balance and any elections you have made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my fund give me default death and incapacity cover` IF
        `the account`'s `I hold a MySuper product`
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `I am a defined benefit member`)
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `I am a permanent or continuous full-time ADF Super member`)
    AND (NOT `the account`'s `I elected not to have death and incapacity cover`)
    AND `May my fund give me insurance cover` `the account`
